# Central pinned refs for vanilla_wow_lab player builds.
#
# One source of truth so wowborg always layers on the SAME deployed shim. Sourced by
# tools/build_player.sh and passed to wowborg/Dockerfile as --build-arg. Pattern follows
# crewrift_lab/tools/versions.env; rationale in
# docs/designs/wowborg-v2-shim-adoption.md ("Image: layer on the deployed artifact").

# The DEPLOYED reference player image wowborg v2 layers on (the "shim"): the exact bytes
# the league runs — king_richard + navmesh helper + Valley-of-Trials mmaps + wow_sdk +
# the vanilla_wow_coworld.player WS wrapper.
#
# DELIBERATELY A DIGEST, not a tag — tags move, digests don't. Provenance:
#   vanilla_wow package 0.1.19 (cow_2788b1c2-45ea-4cc8-ac17-5d54266850f9),
#   manifest player image img_c869afbf-c08d-4192-ae11-12f9acaf04ee,
#   fetched 2026-07-15 via `uv run coworld download vanilla_wow`.
# How you'll know to bump: a new vanilla_wow version appears in `coworld list` (the live
# manifest is the truth — trust it over the game-repo checkout). Then re-run
# `coworld download vanilla_wow`, read the new player-image digest from
# coworld_images.json, update this, rebuild, and re-run the bridge tests (a file-bridge
# schema drift fails loudly via pydantic extra="forbid").
WOWBORG_BASE_IMAGE=public.ecr.aws/q5f4m8t9/cogames@sha256:665adff0b58aeb36b5ac56ab084866888301147be6b28fc09b2c7b5b0a51a193
